    "title": "Perplexity is exponentiated average surprise",
    "description": "Perplexity exponentiates average token-level cross-entropy: PP=2^H for cross-entropy in bits, equivalently the inverse geometric mean of the held-out token probabilities. Lower is better only when comparing on the same test set and vocabulary."
